 pnpm lint            # eslint and the type check, the template's files too
 ```
 
-The template is in [`template/`](https://github.com/comp-markdown/compmd/tree/main/npm-packages/create-pack/template): the files every pack has, those of a leaf or a code renderer, and a library pack's own. Its names are `__pack__`, `__component__`, `__language__` and `__library__`, which are valid in code, so its files are linted, type-checked and tested in place (the components in happy-dom, as `compmd-pack test` runs them), but a library pack's `src/index.ts`, which imports the library only a written pack has.
